  "summary": "Malicious code in tinkoff-boxy-desktop-icons-horizontal (npm)",
  "details": "On require(), the package fingerprints the host OS and architecture (linux/x64, darwin/arm64, win32/x64, etc.) and downloads a platform-specific binary from Cloudflare Workers C2 infrastructure (oob-worker[.]cf103-070[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf100-416[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf102-baf[.]workers[.]dev) via HTTPS GET to paths like /pkg/package, /pkg/package-arm64, /pkg/loader_mac, or /pkg/package.exe. If the HTTPS download fails, it falls back to a DNS TXT-based chunked download from *.dl[.]well1[.]site domains. The downloaded binary is written to /var/tmp/.cache_\u0026lt;random\u0026gt; (Linux/macOS) or %TEMP%\\dotnet_diag_\u0026lt;random\u0026gt;.exe (Windows) and executed as a detached background process. A cache marker file prevents re-download for approximately 6.3 hours.",
